# Who reviews changes to what.
#
# Replace fiwon123 below with the GitHub handle(s) that should
# review this project. Then AGENTS.md's `ASSIGNEE` should match, so the branch
# naming, commit comments, and PR assignee all point at the same person.
#
# Requires "Allow this repository to assign pull requests to reviewers" in
# Settings -> General -> Pull Requests. Without it, GitHub silently ignores
# these rules and nothing is enforced.
#
# Format: <path-pattern>  <reviewer> [<reviewer> ...]
# Last matching pattern wins, so put broad rules first and specific ones last.

# Default: everything requires a review.
* @fiwon123

# Narrow the rules only where you actually want different handling.
# Examples:
#
#   /backend/**            @fiwon123
#   /frontend/**           @fiwon123
#
#   # CI changes need a second pair of eyes
#   /.github/workflows/**  @fiwon123 @fiwon123
#
#   # Agents and instructions drive the whole workflow -- review these carefully
#   /.opencode/**          @fiwon123
#
#   # Ignore generated noise
#   /package-lock.json     @fiwon123